This product includes third-party data and software:

IP geolocation data by DB-IP (https://db-ip.com), licensed under CC BY 4.0.

Cloud provider IPv4 ranges: AWS IP ranges (https://ip-ranges.amazonaws.com/ip-ranges.json)
and Google Cloud IP ranges (https://www.gstatic.com/ipranges/cloud.json), used to
identify a server's provider region.

Hosting-network prefixes: derived at build time from the RIPE Stat API
(https://stat.ripe.net, RIPE NCC) for a curated list of hosting ASNs.

Server city labels: operator geofeed data published by the operators below in
their public RFC 8805 geofeeds, each shown as-is with attribution and the feed's
as-of date. No MaxMind/GeoLite2 data is used or redistributed. An operator can
request removal of its feed or prefixes through the takedown list in
infra/geo/geofeeds/deny.txt; the build drops them and the shipped table is
regenerated without them.

  * G-Core Labs S.A. - https://geofeed.gcore.lu/IP-Range.csv
  * Hetzner Online GmbH - https://www.hetzner.com/geofeed.csv
  * DigitalOcean, LLC - https://www.digitalocean.com/geo/google.csv
  * The Constant Company, LLC (Vultr) - https://geofeed.constant.com/
  * Akamai Connected Cloud (Linode) - https://ipgeo.akamai.com/linode-geofeed.csv
  * Contabo GmbH - https://geofeed.contabo.de/geofeed.csv
  * Equinix Metal (Equinix, Inc.) - https://geofeed.equinixmetal.com/geofeed.csv

Uses the maxminddb crate (MIT licensed).
